  'fs.mkstemp': `
creates and opens a unique temporary file
tmpl: the template string, which must end in 'XXXXXX' (six X's)
returns the actual file name and the file descriptor on success, an empty string and fd=-1 on failure
Note: the order is (name, fd) rather than (fd, name), because the lastBuiltinExtra mechanism requires
the second return value to be an i64/bool and a str to be the primary return value
name: the file name actually created (the last six X's of the template are replaced with random characters; empty string on failure)
