  'fs.open-dir': `
open-dir: opens a directory to read entries
paired with read-dir to read entries one by one; must close-dir when done.
⚠ POSIX directory entries returned one by one by read-dir **include** '.' and '..':
recursive traversal/deletion that accidentally enters '..' escapes upward and may delete the parent tree.
to safely get a "child list" use fs.dir-entries instead (already filters '.'/'..').
p: directory path (cannot be opened if missing or without read permission)
dirp: directory handle for read-dir/close-dir (0=open failed)
`
