  'net': `
net — network operations

provides TCP network programming capabilities, including server listening, client connection, data send/receive.
implemented on top of the POSIX socket API (socket/bind/listen/accept/connect/send/recv).
supports AES-256-GCM encrypted channels, providing end-to-end encryption for plaintext TCP connections.

usage:
// TCP server
l = listen-on('127.0.0.1', 8080)         // returns ?listener
l: {
nil -> return
-> c = l.accept()                      // returns ?conn
}
n = c.recv(buf, 1024)
n = c.send('hello')
c.close()
l.close()

// TCP client
c = dial-to('127.0.0.1', 8080)           // returns ?conn
n = c.send('hello')
n = c.recv(buf, 1024)
c.close()

// encrypted channel
key [32]byte = [...]  // shared key
ec = enc-conn{}
ec.init(c, key)
ec.send-encrypted('sensitive data')
msg = ec.recv-encrypted()  // returns ?str
`
