  'noml': 'noml — NOML config file parsing and generation\n\nNOML is the configuration format of the Nolang toolchain (package.noml / workspace.noml /\nnolang.lock.noml / language packs locales/*.noml).\n\nNOML is literally **valid Nolang literal syntax**: objects `{...}`, arrays `[...]`,\nsingle-quoted strings `\'...\'`, bare numbers, booleans `true`/`false`, and Nolang\'s `nil`\n(**there is no `null`** — the Nolang "empty value" is `nil`). So a NOML document can be\nparsed at runtime by this module, and also read directly as Nolang literals by the compiler. Syntax essentials:\n- The top level is usually an object: `{` and `}` each on their own line, one member per line, newline as separator, no commas.\n- Keys: bare identifiers (starting with an underscore or a lowercase letter; may contain lowercase letters, digits, hyphens),\nwritten as single-quoted strings when they do not conform to the rules.\n- Values: single-quoted strings (`\\\'` `\\\\` `\\/` `\\n` `\\r` `\\t` `\\0` `\\uXXXX`), backtick\nraw strings, true/false/nil, bare numbers, objects, arrays (comma-separated, trailing comma allowed).\n- Comments: `;` to end of line.\n- Annotation markers: `#{key = value, ...}` may only appear on a line of their own above a member, or in the\ntrailing position on the same line as the member; placing it before a member on the same line is a syntax error.\n\nusage:\nr = noml.parse(\'{\\nname: \\\'nolang\\\'\\n}\')\nr: {\nok -> {\nv, found = it.get-str(it.root(), \'name\')\nfound -> print(v)\n}\nerr -> print(it)\n}\n\nThe tree is addressed by "node index" rather than returning child handles like json does. A `doc` contains a\nnode pool (a `#{inline=false}` pointer field); `get` returns an i64 index. Indices are cheaper than handles,\nand avoid the aliasing problem of "parent and child handles each holding a vec header, sharing the same data buffer".\n\nThe raw `#{...}` annotation text on a member (excluding `#{` and `}`) is stored with the node; `ann` reads it back,\n`set-ann` writes it; `ann-value` extracts a value from the annotation by key. On serialization the annotation is output\non a separate line above the member, so `parse` → `stringify` round-trips completely.'
  'noml.doc': `
doc: a NOML document (node pool + root node index)
usage:
d = noml.new()
k = d.new-str('nolang')
o = d.new-obj()
d.put(o, 'name', k)
d.set-root(o)
print(d.stringify())
`
  'noml.doc.ann': `
Gets the root node's `#{...}` annotation raw text
v: ok=annotation raw text, nil=root has no annotation
`
  'noml.doc.ann-value': `
Gets the value of a key in the root node's annotation
key: annotation key
v: ok=value, nil=key does not exist
`
  'noml.doc.at': `
Gets the node index of a root array element by position
i: element index (0-based)
child: ok=element node index, nil=root is not an array or index out of range
`
  'noml.doc.bool': `
gets the root's boolean value
v: ok=boolean value, nil=root is not boolean
`
  'noml.doc.get': `
gets the node index of a root object member by key
key: key name
child: ok=child node index, nil=root is not an object or the key does not exist
`
  'noml.doc.get-bool': `
gets the boolean value of a root object member by key
key: key name
v: ok=boolean value, nil=key missing or value not boolean
`
  'noml.doc.get-f64': `
Gets the numeric value of a root object member by key
key: key name
v: ok=numeric value, nil=key does not exist or value is not a number
`
  'noml.doc.get-i64': `
Gets the integer value of a root object member by key (truncates decimals)
key: key name
v: ok=integer, nil=key not found or value is not a number
`
  'noml.doc.get-str': `
Gets the string value of a root object member by key
key: key name
v: ok=string content, nil=key not found or value is not a string
`
  'noml.doc.has': `
whether the root object has the key
key: key name
found: true=exists
`
  'noml.doc.i64': `
get the root's integer value (truncating decimals)
v: ok=integer, nil=root is not a number
`
  'noml.doc.is-arr': `
whether the root is an array
yes: true=root is an array
`
  'noml.doc.is-bool': `
whether the root is a boolean
yes: true=root is a boolean
`
  'noml.doc.is-nil': `
whether the root is nil
yes: true=root is nil
`
  'noml.doc.is-num': `
Whether the root is a number
yes: true=the root is a number
`
  'noml.doc.is-obj': `
Whether the root is an object
yes: true=root is an object
`
  'noml.doc.is-str': `
Whether the root is a string
yes: true=root is a string
`
  'noml.doc.key': `
Gets the key name of a root object member by position
i: member index (0-based, in file order)
key: ok=key name, nil=root is not an object or index out of range
`
  'noml.doc.kind': `
Root node kind
k: NOML-KIND-*; NOML-KIND-NIL when the root is invalid
`
  'noml.doc.len': `
number of child elements of the root node (object member count or array length)
n: number of child elements
`
  'noml.doc.new-arr': `
Create an empty array node
idx: new node index
`
  'noml.doc.new-bool': `
creates a boolean node
v: boolean value to store in the node
idx: index of the new node in the pool, for the caller to attach subtrees
`
  'noml.doc.new-nil': `
Creates a nil node
