  'process.process-fork': `
forks the current process
returns 0 = child, >0 = parent (the child PID), -1 = error
pid: fork result (0=child process, >0=child PID, -1=error)
`
  'process.process-getppid': `
gets the parent process ID
pid: parent process ID
`
  'process.process-kill': `
sends a signal to a process
pid: target process ID
sig: signal number (e.g. SIG-KILL=9)
ok: whether the signal was sent successfully
`
  'process.process-pipe': `
creates a pipe
returns the packed value (read_fd << 32) | write_fd
fds: the packed pipe descriptors (read_fd<<32)|write_fd (<0=error)
`
  'process.process-shell': `
alternative:
out, stderr, code, err = process.cmd('ls', args, '', '', env, 5000, false)  ; full featured
pid = process.spawn(cmd)                                        ; non-blocking
status = process.wait(pid)                                      ; returns the real exit code
