Parse the HTTP request (received over TLS)
returns ok: true = parsed successfully
`
  'server.https-server-conn.recv-more': `
Receive more data from the TLS connection into recv-buf
returns n: bytes received (-1 = error, 0 = connection closed)
`
  'server.https-server-conn.reset': 'Reset connection state for reuse (Keep-Alive)'
  'server.https-server-conn.write-body': `
Write the response body (over TLS)
data: response body data
returns ok: true = success
`
  'server.https-server-conn.write-header': `
Write a single response header (over TLS)
name: header name
value: header value
returns ok: true = success
`
  'server.https-server-conn.write-headers-done': `
Write the empty line marking the end of headers (over TLS)
returns ok: true = success
`
  'server.https-server-conn.write-html': `
Convenience method — write an HTML response (over TLS)
status: HTTP response status code (e.g. 200, 404)
html: HTML content
returns ok: true = success
`
  'server.https-server-conn.write-json': `
Convenience method — write a JSON response (over TLS)
status: HTTP response status code (e.g. 200, 404)
json-str: JSON string
returns ok: true = success
`
  'server.https-server-conn.write-status': `
Write the HTTP status line (over TLS)
status: HTTP status code (e.g. 200, 404); the reason phrase is mapped internally and written as "HTTP/1.1 <status> <reason>\r\n", unknown codes default to 'OK'
returns ok: true = success
`
