  'str.split': `
splits the string into substrings on a separator
sep: split substring; the input is cut at every occurrence and sep itself does not enter the result
returns out: the resulting substrings
An empty separator returns the whole string as the single element
Note: it builds a local result slice and assigns it to out, working around a compiler bug where out.push on an output parameter does not take effect
