  'tls.tls-pad': `
TLS 1.2 CBC padding (RFC 5246 §6.2.3.2) — different from PKCS#7!
The padding is pad-count bytes total, each valued pad-count - 1 (the final length byte equals pad-count-1).
A peer (e.g. OpenSSL) reads the last byte P, removes P+1 bytes, and requires all P+1 bytes to equal P.
If PKCS#7 were used instead (value = pad-count), when the plaintext is already a whole number of blocks it would pad 16 bytes of 0x10,
and the peer would try to remove 17 bytes, running into the trailing MAC bytes → bad record mac.
in: plaintext (content || MAC)
returns out: padded data (length a multiple of 16)
`
  'tls.tls-sig-rsa-pkcs1-sha256': 'Signature algorithms'
  'tls.tls-unpad': `
TLS 1.2 CBC unpadding
in: decrypted data (content || MAC || padding)
returns out-n: length after removing padding (content+MAC), -1 = padding error
`
