  'yaml.parser.merge-into': `
Handling of the merge key << (supports a mapping or a sequence of mappings)
keys: list of key node indices of the target mapping
vals: list of value node indices of the target mapping
src: value node index of the merge key (<<) (MAP or sequence of MAPs)
ok-keys: merged key list
ok-vals: merged value list
`
  'yaml.parser.merge-one': `
Merge the entries of one mapping into keys/vals (without overwriting existing keys)
note: the MIR backend does not allow moving an input vec directly into another vec (borrow/ownership protection),
so this copies element by element instead of ok-keys = keys.
keys: list of key node indices of the target mapping
vals: list of value node indices of the target mapping
src: index of the mapping node to merge (must be of MAP kind)
ok-keys: merged key list (existing keys take precedence)
ok-vals: merged value list
`
  'yaml.parser.newline': `
consumes one newline (\n or \r\n)
yes: consumed one newline; false=not at a newline, position unchanged
